<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23228" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαιμον-ίζομαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαιμονάω, ἄλλος κατ᾽ ἄλλην
					δαιμονίζεται τύχην</span>
			 each one hath his own <i>fate appointed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				191
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be deified,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				173
			</span></i> (so expld. by <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				90
			</span></i>; 
				Act.
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>to be possessed by a demon</i> or <i>evil spirit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Matt.
				4.24
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.706d
			</span></i>.</div>
